# Language — ironclad

**Russian exists in exactly one place: live chat between an agent and Yury.**
That is the only exception. Token thrift is the reason: rules, cards, comments,
scripts, and reports stay English so every agent rereads one language.

**Everything else is English. Always. Existing and new.**
If leftover Russian is found, translate it or rename the file. Do not leave
Cyrillic in the repo “because it is old”.

| Surface | Language |
|---|---|
| Live chat answers to Yury | Russian |
| Rule files (`.mdc`), agent profiles, task cards | English |
| Code comments (C#, PowerShell, Python, Bash, …) | English |
| `[Header]`, `[Tooltip]`, Inspector text | English |
| `Debug.Log` / `Write-Host` / overlay / exceptions | English |
| `DOCS.md`, `CURRENT.md`, READMEs, trial narrative `.md` | English |
| Git commit messages | English |
| Agent-to-agent notes in the project | English |
| File and folder names | English (rename leftovers) |

Do not put Russian — including quotes and examples — inside a rule, card,
agent profile, README, or source file.

# What must not be translated

Class names, function names, variables, Unity API names, CLI arguments, and
metric names stay in their original English/code form (`FixedUpdate`,
`Rigidbody2D`, `HingeJoint2D`, `fell`, `pelvisDrop`).

Do not rename historical trial labels or baseline folder names
(`Trials/Baselines/stable-pd/`, run ids). Those are identifiers, not prose.

Do not rewrite historical `Trials/Runs/*.json` / `*.csv` payloads. They are
stand records, not documents.

# Comments

New comments explain why and the physical meaning; they do not restate the
line. A leftover Russian comment is not “existing style” — translate it.

When editing any project file, the result must contain no Cyrillic.
